<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa Elena Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santa Elena is a province on the Pacific coast of Ecuador, covering the Santa Elena peninsula, the westernmost part of the country's coast. It was separated from Guayas province in 2007. The peninsula has early archaeological sites such as Real Alto of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdivia">Valdivia</a> culture, an old oil field at Ancón and the beach resort of Salinas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santa-elena-province.jpg" alt="Santa Elena Province" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: dave kess · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_beach_punta_carnero_ecuador_sunset.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
